{"availability":"available","full":"ornew/pego","name":"pego","description":"PEGO: Parser Framework","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2023-07-29T06:00:40Z","updated":"2026-10-16T18:21:09Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pego.ornew.net","topics":[],"demo":"https://pego.ornew.net/playground/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:48.511Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:48.511Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T21:31:48.511Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:19:59.475Z","stars":3,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T21:31:48.511Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Blazing fast. Runs anywhere. Streams forever. Reparses in a blink.","Website · Playground · Quick start · Guides · Specification · Examples","PEGO turns one grammar file into a production parser. The grammar language extends Parsing Expression Grammars with types, operator precedence, left recursion and error recovery, so a single .pego file defines both the syntax and the tree you get back. Run it on the engine, on a portable bytecode VM, or as generated code with zero dependencies — the result is the same everywhere."],"features":["Edits in a blink. Document reparses only what an edit touched: about 1 ms after a one-character edit to an","Infinite input, flat memory. ParseStream emits each element as soon as it matches and drops the input it","Write once, run anywhere. Grammars compile to a language-independent bytecode with a","Fast out of the box. A 262 KB JSON document becomes a fully typed, positioned tree in about 3 ms with a","Every backend, one answer. Closure engine, recursive VM, iterative VM, generated Go and TypeScript: the test"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ornew/pego/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d872faf80498e3d481041966e57e0752ce6f61023a051009c891b4a88e36fc7f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T23:19:59.550Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10